packages/e2e/.e2e-data/

# Local worker tarballs from scripts/pack-worker.mjs (never committed)
dist-worker-pack/

# Server process telemetry written into DATA_DIR (= packages/server in a checkout): the
# liveness heartbeat and the append-only exit log from lib/exit-record.ts. Machine state,
# regenerated every boot — a tracked copy would show up as a dirty tree on every run and
# block auto-merge.
packages/server/process-alive.json
packages/server/process-exit-log.jsonl

# test-impact outcome ledger (#954): one append-only JSONL row per pre-merge gate run, written by
# the gate so `impact.mjs stats` can report a measured MISS RATE for the selection heuristic.
# Deliberately gitignored and per-machine (decided on #954) — the alternatives were a CI artifact
# or a committed file that churns in every diff. Accepted cost: outcomes are lost on a fresh clone
# and not shared with CI; on a single-machine board that is where the gate runs anyway, and
# `record --source` already tags rows by origin so two files can be merged later if that changes.
# IGNORED, not merely untracked: an untracked-but-unignored file in the main checkout is exactly
# the shape that makes `getDirtyMainFiles` block every subsequent merge.
.test-impact/
